This is a complete guide to building a full-stack MERN application (MongoDB, Express, React, Node.js).

I will create a simple **"Task Manager"** where you can:
1.  Create dummy data via the API.
2.  Create new tasks via the frontend.
3.  View all tasks.

---

### Prerequisites
*   **Node.js** installed.
*   **MongoDB** installed (or a MongoDB Atlas connection string).
*   A code editor (VS Code).

---

### Part 1: The Backend (Node.js & Express)

#### 1. Setup the Project
Open your terminal and create a folder for your project:

```bash
mkdir fullstack-app
cd fullstack-app
mkdir backend
cd backend
npm init -y
npm install express mongoose cors
npm install --save-dev nodemon
```

#### 2. Create `backend/index.js`
This file handles the server, the database connection, and the dummy data.

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const mongoose = require('mongoose');
const cors = require('cors');

const app = express();
const PORT = 5000;

// Middleware
app.use(cors()); // Allow frontend to talk to backend
app.use(express.json());

// 1. Database Connection
// Replace with your local URI or Atlas URI
mongoose.connect('mongodb://localhost:27017/taskmanager', {
    useNewUrlParser: true,
    useUnifiedTopology: true
}).then(() => console.log("MongoDB Connected"))
  .catch(err => console.log(err));

// 2. Define Schema
const TaskSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
    title: String,
    description: String,
    completed: { type: Boolean, default: false },
    createdAt: { type: Date, default: Date.now }
});

const Task = mongoose.model('Task', TaskSchema);

// 3. Helper to Create Dummy Data
const createDummyData = async () => {
    try {
        // Check if data exists to avoid duplicates
        const count = await Task.countDocuments();
        if (count === 0) {
            const dummyTasks = [
                { title: 'Learn Node.js', description: 'Understand the basics', completed: false },
                { title: 'Build an API', description: 'Use Express', completed: true },
                { title: 'Connect to DB', description: 'Use Mongoose', completed: true },
            ];
            await Task.insertMany(dummyTasks);
            console.log("✅ Dummy Data Created!");
        }
    } catch (error) {
        console.error("Error creating dummy data:", error);
    }
};

